{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Independent corroboration from AWS CloudTrail (cross-source log audit, 2026-07-30). These are server-side records of the `bedrock:Converse` calls themselves, so they confirm the error text and exact timing independently of anything we logged locally.\n\nEvery `Converse` call in the account in July occurred today; 14 of 31 carried an errorCode. The 11 `ValidationException`s were all made under `user/joe_frontier`:\n\n    2026-07-30T16:03:39Z  Invocation of model ID anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 with on-demand\n                          throughput isn't supported. Retry your request with the ID or ARN\n                          of an inference profile.\n    2026-07-30T20:34:19Z  The model returned the following errors: `temperature` is deprecated for this model.\n    2026-07-30T20:34:21Z  The model returned the following errors: `temperature` is deprecated for this model.\n    2026-07-30T20:34:23Z  The provided model identifier is invalid.        (x4 in the same second)\n    2026-07-30T20:34:23Z  The model returned the following errors: `temperature` is deprecated for this model.\n    2026-07-30T20:35:01Z  The model returned the following errors: `temperature` is deprecated for this model.\n    2026-07-30T20:35:01Z  The model returned the following errors: `temperature` is deprecated for this model.\n    2026-07-30T20:35:04Z  The model returned the following errors: `top_p` is deprecated for this model.\n\nTwo things this adds beyond what the ticket already records:\n\n1. The `top_p` variant is confirmed as a real server-side rejection (a single occurrence, 20:35:04Z), not merely inferred from the `temperature` case. Both parameters are rejected by the same class of model.\n2. `The provided model identifier is invalid` fired 4x within one second at 20:34:23Z, interleaved with the `temperature` rejections. That is a distinct failure from the deprecation errors and may indicate the override-table miss and an id-resolution miss are being hit on the same code path. Worth confirming they are two bugs, not one, before scoping the fix. (Possibly relevant to 281f, where `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` is parsed but read by nothing.)\n\nSeparately, and NOT part of this bug: the same CloudTrail sweep shows 3x `AccessDenied` on `bedrock:Converse` at 16:59:59Z, 17:01:28Z and 17:02:09Z under `arn:aws:sts::896586841071:assumed-role/rebar-gerrit-instance-role/i-00880b2c7f13527c5` — the production box. That belongs to story 9249 (grant the review-bot Bedrock access), noted here only so the two are not conflated when reading the timeline.\n\nMethod: `aws cloudtrail lookup-events --lookup-attributes AttributeKey=EventName,AttributeValue=Converse` over 2026-07-01 -> 07-30, us-east-1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785451637283185001,"uuid":"b3620a29-5e0d-4ebd-9817-6161e04231ff"}